A wrong submission is evidence against the transformation hypothesis as a whole. Do not respond by changing a few guessed cells while preserving an unverified premise. Re-read the full demonstrations and list plausible rule families, then compare complete-grid predictions coordinate-by-coordinate, including untouched background, marker retention, orientation, and extent. If the remaining hypotheses predict different outputs on a new example, spend a demo request; otherwise submit only the best-supported complete prediction.

